  m_text: 'Step-Up End User License Agreement (EULA)


    1. Acceptance of Terms

    By
    creating an account and using the Step-Up application, you acknowledge that you
    have read, understood, and agree to be bound by these terms. If you do not agree,
    do not use this application.


    2. Academic Project & Expert Consultation
    Disclaimer

    Step-Up is developed as an academic capstone simulation project.
    While the application features fitness guidelines and proper posture techniques
    developed in direct consultation with a verified medical doctor and fitness experts,
    the application itself is NOT a certified medical device. The information provided
    is for educational and tracking purposes. You use this application entirely at
    your own risk.


    3. Data Collection & GPS Tracking

    To function properly,
    Step-Up requires continuous access to your device''s pedometer (physical activity
    sensors) and background location (GPS) to track your physical movement and map
    your avatar to real-world coordinates.


    4. Data Storage & Privacy

    Your
    login credentials, step counts, and location history are transmitted to and stored
    securely on Firebase databases. We prioritize your privacy. This data will only
    be used for the evaluation of this academic project and will never be sold, rented,
    or distributed to third-party marketing agencies or advertisers.


    5. Physical
    Health Warning & Posture Safety

    Step-Up provides expert-backed recommendations
    for proper posture and safe movement. However, this general guidance does not
    replace personalized medical advice. Always consult with your own qualified healthcare
    provider before starting any new exercise program or strenuous fitness routine.
    If you experience faintness, dizziness, pain, or shortness of breath at any time
    while walking or using Step-Up, stop immediately.


    6. User Conduct

    Users
    agree to remain aware of their physical surroundings while using the application.
    Do not trespass on private property or enter dangerous areas (such as active
    roadways) to interact with the map.


    7. Account Termination

    The developers
    reserve the right to delete accounts, reset step counters, or terminate server
    access at any time without notice, particularly upon the completion of the academic
    evaluation period.


    Check the box below to acknowledge that you have read
    and accept these terms.'
